"router": "(1) routing by keyword \u2014 the happy path\n    billing   <- matched 'invoice'\n    code      <- matched 'bug'\n    research  <- matched 'paper'\n\n(2) now a paraphrase the table was never given\n    fallback  <- matched None\n    a human reads that as a CODE problem instantly.\n    'compile' is in the table; 'won't build' is not. No meaning, only text.\n\n(3) the seam: the rule table is injectable\n    code      <- matched \"won't build\"\n    patched in one line \u2014 and that is exactly the treadmill a real\n    triage agent takes off you.\n\nVERDICT: fallback is a routing decision, not a bug \u2014 but keyword routing cannot generalise",
"hitl": "(1) a sensitive action reaches the gate\n    status=awaiting_approval  performed=False\n    the action has NOT run; the run is parked in the checkpoint store\n\n(2) a human approves, in time\n       >> REFUND ISSUED\n    approved: human approved; action performed\n\n(3) a human rejects\n    rejected: human rejected; action not performed\n\n(4) a human approves \u2014 but two hours late\n    timed_out: approval deadline exceeded (7200s > 60s)\n    the deadline is checked BEFORE the decision, so a late yes is void\n\n    refunds actually issued: 1 of 3 requests\n\nVERDICT: approved / rejected / timed out \u2014 and only the first one moves money",
